<title>GERMANY: Hoechst sells unit to Dutch group.</title>
<headline>Hoechst sells unit to Dutch group.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group Hoechst AG said on Thursday that it had sold its Dutch Trespa International B.V. unit to a unit of Dutch investment group HAL Holding NV  HLAN.F for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>The unit, which makes decorative high-pressure laminates for the construction and interior design industry and employs 450 people, was part of Hoechst Holland N.V. It was sold to HAL Investments B.V. effective from Thursday, Hoechst said in a statement.</p>
<p>Hoechst has been spinning off a number of businesses recently in a bid to concentrate on its core business and boost shareholder value.</p>
</text>
